{"profile":{"name":"Dianne Saxe","ward":"Ward 11, University—Rosedale","bio":"Dianne Saxe was elected to Toronto City Council in October 2022 and took office on November 15, 2022, representing Ward 11 University—Rosedale, succeeding Mike Layton. An environmental and energy lawyer, she was Ontario's third and last Environmental Commissioner (2015–2019) before the office was abolished, and served as Deputy Leader of the Green Party of Ontario from 2020 to 2022 before resigning to run as an independent. She sits on Council as an independent and serves as the Mayor's Environmental Champion. Ahead of the October 26, 2026 municipal election, she withdrew her Ward 11 re-election candidacy in August 2026 and registered instead in Ward 14 Toronto—Danforth following Paula Fletcher's retirement announcement.","committees":["Infrastructure and Environment Committee","Toronto and East York Community Council","TTC Board","Toronto Hydro Corporation Board of Directors","Toronto Atmospheric Fund Board of Directors","Toronto and Region Conservation Authority","National Zero Waste Council Management Board","Mayor's Environmental Champion"],"contact":{"email":"Councillor_Saxe@toronto.ca","phone":"416-392-4009"},"promises":[{"text":"Enforce a Vacant Home Tax to reduce speculators.","source":"https://storeys.com/toronto-new-city-councillor-elects/"},{"text":"Build the city \"in and up,\" mitigating urban sprawl with more middle housing in all residential zones.","source":"https://storeys.com/toronto-new-city-councillor-elects/"},{"text":"Fund a revolving loan fund for non-profit housing providers.","source":"https://storeys.com/toronto-new-city-councillor-elects/"}]},"lobbying":{"total":741,"term":741,"first":"2022-11-17","last":"2026-10-08","lobbyists":104,"clients":101,"subjects":229,"methods":{"Meetings":189,"Emails":416,"Phone calls":85,"Written":12,"Other or unreported":39},"top":[{"label":"Building Permits","count":188},{"label":"Planning and Development","count":183},{"label":"Pla